// Title: Deleted Data Overwritten Via Cipher.EXE
// Sigma ID: 4b046706-5789-4673-b111-66f25fe99534
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-12-26 | Modified: 2023-02-21
// ATT&CK: impact, T1485
// Description: Detects usage of the "cipher" built-in utility in order to overwrite deleted data from disk.
//   Adversaries may destroy data and files on specific systems or in large numbers on a network to
//   interrupt availability to systems, services, and network resources. Data destruction is likely
//   to render stored data irrecoverable by forensic techniques through overwriting files or data on
//   local and remote drives
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1485/T1485.md#atomic-test-3---overwrite-deleted-data-on-c-drive
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cipher_overwrite_deleted_data.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "CIPHER.EXE" or FolderPath endswith "\\cipher.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains " /w:"
